{% extends "tool_layout" %}
{% import "tool_macros" as m %}

{% block tool %}
{{ m.panel("reverse", "Reverse text", "The reversed text updates as you type.",
    "Enter text to reverse...", "Reversed text") }}
{% endblock %}

{% block about %}
<h2 class="h4">How it works</h2>
<p>The order of the characters is flipped, so <code>Hello, world!</code> becomes <code>!dlrow ,olleH</code>.
    Line breaks are reversed too, so the last line comes first.</p>
<p>Characters are reversed the way you see them. Emoji with skin tones, family emoji, flags and letters with
    separate accent marks stay intact instead of being split into broken pieces, which happens with simpler
    reverse-text tools.</p>

<h2 class="h4">What people use it for</h2>
<p>Checking palindromes, writing puzzles and mirror text for games, quick tests of how software handles
    unusual input, and simple text effects for social media.</p>
{% endblock %}
